  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\Gamma$ be a graph that is not a nontrivial join, and let $A(\\Gamma)$\nbe the associated right-angled Artin group. Does there exist an injective map from\n$A(\\Gamma)$ to the mapping class group of a surface such that every loxodromic element\nof $A(\\Gamma)$ is sent to a pseudo-Anosov mapping class?",
